pplication\u002Fjson",14120,"sha256:66adabb919757be63b4b629b113043b61c24fc65b79fc585ffa48fb092ca132f","2026-11-17T19:24:49Z","https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fs00d\u002Fgs-soft\u002Freleases\u002Fdownload\u002Fv0.9.0\u002Flatest.json","https:\u002F\u002Fapi.github.com\u002Frepos\u002Fs00d\u002Fgs-soft\u002Ftarball\u002Fv0.9.0","https:\u002F\u002Fapi.github.com\u002Frepos\u002Fs00d\u002Fgs-soft\u002Fzipball\u002Fv0.9.0","## Gateway Soft 0.9.0\n\n### New: Gateway Proxy (Android)\n- Turns a phone into a SOCKS5\u002FHTTP proxy whose traffic goes only through the SIM; sold on the marketplace through the proxy-relay server (OpenProxy). The seller enters only an API token.\n- Traffic quota (monthly \u002F daily \u002F manual reset) and speed limits per buyer and for the Wi-Fi port, with optional slow-down near the quota.\n- Self-update from the GitHub release, like Gateway Phone; \"Stop\" in the notification, watchdog restart, vendor autostart settings shortcut.\n- **Known gap:** this build has a placeholder relay address, so selling does not work yet; it will be set in the next release.\n\n### Fixed\n- **Web UI \u002F headless (`--serve`):** silent and slowloris connections are closed after 10–15 s; WebSocket messages are capped at 2 MB; a malformed invoke gets an error reply; a burst of pipelined calls no longer disconnects the client.\n- **Desktop and `--serve`:** SIGTERM shuts down cleanly (ports leave sale, last settings write saved); a leftover `config.json.tmp-*` from a killed writer is removed on start.\n- **SIM back in service** (after PIN\u002FPUK lock or lost coverage) goes back on sale at the next port check instead of after up to 5 minutes of backoff (phone and desktop modems).\n- **Gateway Phone:** no `:core` ANR at start on slow phones; while the app is on screen the core is protected from the low-memory killer like the UI; a late USSD reply never answers the next USSD; SIM inbox overflow no longer stalls receiving; a slow command no longer freezes the UI ↔ core link; an accepted SMS is deleted from the SIM right away (no duplicate after a kill).\n- **Gateway Proxy:** quota usage survives a kill; aborted tunnels are reset; dead relay tunnels after a network change are dropped quickly.\n\n### Also\n- One-command install \u002F update: `curl -fsSL https:\u002F\u002Fs00d.github.io\u002Fgs-soft\u002Finstall.sh | sh`, `irm https:\u002F\u002Fs00d.github.io\u002Fgs-soft\u002Finstall.ps1 | iex`.\n- Documentation site in English, Russian and German; USB-serial drivers page.\n\n### Not verified for this release\nReal modems and carriers, a release build on a real low-end phone, Windows.\n",1794978318657]